    "lawCode": "Amd §1, Chap 392 of 1973",
    "lawSection": "New York State Medical Care Facilities Finance Agency Act",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5450\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the New York state medical care facilities finance\nagency act, in relation to the ability to issue certain bonds and\nnotes\n\n\n PURPOSE OF BILL :\n\nThis bill would increase the authorization of the Dormitory Authority\nof the State of New York (\"DASNY\"), as successor to the New York State\nMedical Care Facilities Finance Agency (\"MCFFA\") pursuant to issue\nhospital and nursing home project bonds and notes from $14.2 billion\ndollars to $15 billion dollars.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of this bill amends the New York State MCFFA Act to increase\nDASNY's authorization to issue hospital and nursing home project bonds\nand notes from $14.2 billion to $15 billion dollars.\n\nSection 2 of this bill sets forth the effective date.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nPresent law provides that the DASNY shall not issue hospital and\nnursing home project bonds and notes in an aggregate principal amount\nexceeding $14.2 billion dollars.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is new legislation.\n\n STATEMENT IN SUPPORT :\n\nDASNY issues bonds for the purpose of funding mortgage loans or\nproject loans to not-for-profit hospital and nursing home\ncorporations. Some of the bonds issued for DASNY's hospital and\nnursing home clients are issued under the MCFFA Act's federally aided\nmortgage loan program, which involves obtaining Federal Housing\nAdministration (\"FHA\") mortgage insurance.\n\nBonds issued pursuant to both of these programs are subject to the\ncurrent hospital and nursing home project bond authorization cap in\nthe MCFFA Act of $14.2 billion. This authorization was most recently\nincreased by $800 million in 2008.\n\nAs of January 6, 2009, DASNY has either authorized the issuance of\nbonds or adopted resolutions to proceed in the maximum amount of\n$422,345,000. Thus, $377,655,000 of capacity under the existing\nstatutory limitation is available for other transactions. There are,\nhowever, currently nine hospital and nursing home financings in the\nAuthority's current \"pipeline\" totaling about $822 million. Without an\nincrease in the \"cap,\" the Authority will be unable to meet the needs\nof these and other clients.\n\nAlthough DASNY cannot predict exactly when these proposed financings\nwill occur, the Authority is seeking additional bond authorization at\nthis time to ensure that it will be able to meet the needs of all its\nprivate not-for-profit health-care clients on a timely basis. Absent\nthe timely enactment of this legislation, some hospital and nursing\nhomes could be required to defer projects that are necessary to enable\nthese institutions to meet the health care needs of those they serve.\n\n BUDGETARY IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
